1
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:12,150
A weather app says there is a 70 per cent chance of rain tomorrow.

2
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:14,370
Your friend says rain is likely.

3
00:00:14,420 --> 00:00:17,760
Your little brother says rain is certain.

4
00:00:17,810 --> 00:00:18,700
Who is right?

5
00:00:18,750 --> 00:00:22,540
Is a 70 per cent chance likely, certain, or unlikely?

6
00:00:22,590 --> 00:00:25,890
Pause the video and decide.

7
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:27,390
Your friend is right.

8
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:32,150
70 per cent is more than an even chance, so rain is likely.

9
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:33,710
But it is not certain.

10
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:38,100
There is still a 30 per cent chance that it stays dry.

11
00:00:38,150 --> 00:00:41,860
Remember: one half is 0.5, or 50 per cent.

12
00:00:41,910 --> 00:00:45,090
One quarter is 0.25, or 25 per cent.

13
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:47,700
And 70 per cent is 0.7.

14
00:00:47,750 --> 00:00:51,470
Probability measures how likely something is to happen.

15
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:54,830
Words help, but numbers are more precise.

16
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:57,320
Impossible means it cannot happen.

17
00:00:57,370 --> 00:00:59,420
Its probability is 0.

18
00:00:59,470 --> 00:01:02,210
Unlikely means less than an even chance.

19
00:01:02,260 --> 00:01:04,940
An even chance is a probability of 0.5.

20
00:01:04,990 --> 00:01:08,150
Likely means more than an even chance.

21
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:08,850
Your turn.

22
00:01:08,900 --> 00:01:13,200
What does a probability of 1 mean: certain, or an even chance?

23
00:01:13,250 --> 00:01:16,490
Pause the video and decide.

24
00:01:16,540 --> 00:01:18,920
A probability of 1 means certain.

25
00:01:18,970 --> 00:01:21,090
The event must happen.

26
00:01:21,140 --> 00:01:24,510
All probabilities sit on a scale from 0 to 1.

27
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:27,640
0 is impossible, and 1 is certain.

28
00:01:27,690 --> 00:01:32,820
You can write a probability as a fraction, a decimal or a percentage.

29
00:01:32,870 --> 00:01:37,910
But a probability is never less than 0, and never more than 1.

30
00:01:37,960 --> 00:01:39,360
Here is the method.

31
00:01:39,410 --> 00:01:41,180
Step 1: ask 3 questions.

32
00:01:41,230 --> 00:01:42,700
Can it never happen?

33
00:01:42,750 --> 00:01:43,840
Must it happen?

34
00:01:43,890 --> 00:01:45,300
Is it 50 50?

35
00:01:45,350 --> 00:01:51,230
Step 2: if not, decide if it is more likely or less likely than an even chance.

36
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:57,070
Step 3: if you have a number, change it to a decimal and place it on the scale.

37
00:01:57,120 --> 00:02:02,260
Step 4: to compare probabilities, write them all in the same form.

38
00:02:02,310 --> 00:02:04,330
Place 3 events on the scale.

39
00:02:04,380 --> 00:02:06,990
First: rolling a 7 on a normal dice.

40
00:02:07,040 --> 00:02:11,280
A dice only has the numbers 1 to 6, so this is impossible.

41
00:02:11,330 --> 00:02:13,380
The probability is 0.

42
00:02:13,430 --> 00:02:15,720
Second: a coin landing on heads.

43
00:02:15,770 --> 00:02:18,310
That is an even chance: 0.5.

44
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:21,330
Third: the day after Monday being Tuesday.

45
00:02:21,380 --> 00:02:22,480
That is certain.

46
00:02:22,530 --> 00:02:24,530
The probability is 1.

47
00:02:24,580 --> 00:02:32,420
Which is more likely: an event with probability 7 tenths, or an event with probability 68 per cent?

48
00:02:32,470 --> 00:02:34,560
Write both as decimals.

49
00:02:34,610 --> 00:02:36,040
7 tenths is 0.7.

50
00:02:36,090 --> 00:02:38,450
68 per cent is 0.68.

51
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:39,550
0.7 is bigger.

52
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:42,220
So 7 tenths is more likely.

53
00:02:42,270 --> 00:02:43,000
Your turn.

54
00:02:43,050 --> 00:02:46,100
Which is more likely: 0.45, or 2 fifths?

55
00:02:46,150 --> 00:02:49,600
Pause the video and try it.

56
00:02:49,650 --> 00:02:51,170
2 fifths is 0.4.

57
00:02:51,220 --> 00:02:53,920
And 0.45 is bigger than 0.4.

58
00:02:53,970 --> 00:02:56,730
So 0.45 is more likely.

59
00:02:56,780 --> 00:03:00,630
Ella says the probability of her team winning is 1.3.

60
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:02,430
Can she be right?

61
00:03:02,480 --> 00:03:02,680
No.

62
00:03:02,730 --> 00:03:05,550
Probabilities are between 0 and 1.

63
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:08,040
And 1.3 is more than 1.

64
00:03:08,090 --> 00:03:12,690
Put these events in order, from least likely to most likely.

65
00:03:12,740 --> 00:03:14,480
A has probability 0.55.

66
00:03:14,530 --> 00:03:16,570
B has probability 3 fifths.

67
00:03:16,620 --> 00:03:19,440
C has probability 52 per cent.

68
00:03:19,490 --> 00:03:24,560
Write them all as decimals: 0.55, 0.6 and 0.52.

69
00:03:24,610 --> 00:03:28,180
The smallest is 0.52, then 0.55, then 0.6.

70
00:03:28,230 --> 00:03:30,790
So the order is C, A, B.

71
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:33,650
A bag has 4 red sweets and 7 blue sweets.

72
00:03:33,700 --> 00:03:36,580
Find the probability of picking a red one.

73
00:03:36,630 --> 00:03:38,110
Here is Ali's working.

74
00:03:38,160 --> 00:03:40,610
Which line goes wrong first?

75
00:03:40,660 --> 00:03:41,770
Line 2 is wrong.

76
00:03:41,820 --> 00:03:45,750
7 over 4 is more than 1, so it cannot be a probability.

77
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:50,780
Divide the number of red sweets by the total number of sweets.

78
00:03:50,830 --> 00:03:53,250
There are 11 sweets altogether.

79
00:03:53,300 --> 00:03:56,670
The probability of red is 4 over 11.

80
00:03:56,720 --> 00:04:00,100
Weather forecasters use probability every day.

81
00:04:00,150 --> 00:04:07,350
A 70 per cent chance of rain means: on 10 days like this one, it rains on about 7 of them.

82
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:12,900
A football match starts with a coin toss, because each captain has an even chance.

83
00:04:12,950 --> 00:04:14,740
That makes it fair.

84
00:04:14,790 --> 00:04:20,260
And doctors talk about risk in the same way: a number between 0 and 1.

85
00:04:20,310 --> 00:04:21,630
One last question.

86
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:27,480
Which of these is a valid probability: 3 quarters, 4 thirds, or 110 per cent?

87
00:04:27,530 --> 00:04:30,930
Pause the video and decide.

88
00:04:30,980 --> 00:04:31,820
3 quarters.

89
00:04:31,870 --> 00:04:33,610
It is between 0 and 1.

90
00:04:33,660 --> 00:04:36,850
The other 2 are both more than 1.

91
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:41,820
To remember: probability goes from 0, impossible, to 1, certain.

92
00:04:41,870 --> 00:04:44,080
0.5 is an even chance.

93
00:04:44,130 --> 00:04:49,370
The words are: impossible, unlikely, even chance, likely and certain.

94
00:04:49,420 --> 00:04:54,040
Write probabilities as fractions, decimals or percentages.

95
00:04:54,090 --> 00:04:58,340
A probability is never below 0, and never above 1.

96
00:04:58,390 --> 00:05:03,790
Great work! Now practise lesson 13.1 on Camday.
